### Every operator on the PostgREST allow-list, one request each, against the seeded seven rows.
### Each one is asserted as the exact SET of references it returns, never as "the request succeeded":
### a 200 carrying the wrong rows is the failure this group exists to catch.
# @name Eq
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?reference=eq.WO-1003&limit=100
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

###
# @name Neq
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?status=neq.completed&limit=100
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

###
# @name Gt
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?priority=gt.2&limit=100
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

###
# @name Gte
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?priority=gte.3&limit=100
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

###
# @name Lt
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?priority=lt.2&limit=100
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

###
# @name Lte
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?priority=lte.1&limit=100
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

### `like` is case-SENSITIVE, and the pair below is what proves it rather than asserting it
# @name Like
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?title=like.%25repair&limit=100
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

### The same pattern in the wrong case: `like` must return nothing where `ilike` returns the row
# @name LikeWrongCase
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?title=like.%25REPAIR&limit=100
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

###
# @name ILike
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?title=ilike.%25REPAIR&limit=100
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

###
# @name In
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?reference=in.(WO-1001,WO-1007,WO-4242)&limit=100
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

### `is` over a null: five of the seven rows carry no `scheduled_for`
# @name IsNull
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?scheduled_for=is.null&limit=100
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

### `is` over a boolean, which SQL's own IS accepts and `eq` would answer differently for nulls
# @name IsTrue
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?is_emergency=is.true&limit=100
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

### Several parameters are one conjunction, PostgREST's own reading — a filter only ever narrows
# @name TwoParametersConjoin
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?status=eq.completed&priority=eq.3&limit=100
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}

### An operator spelling that is not on the allow-list is refused, never quietly read as `eq`
# @name UnknownOperator
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [422]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?priority=between.1
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{keyDispatcherNorth}}
